WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.360
What if the Roblox AI assistant could remember&nbsp;
exactly how you want it to work? With the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:11.200
custom skills feature, you can give it reusable&nbsp;
instructions for your coding style, workflows, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:18.320
repeatable tasks. These skills can also be used&nbsp;
with supported AI tools outside of Roblox Studio. I'm going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.920
to be showing you two different ways to create&nbsp;
your own skill directly inside of Roblox Studio.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:30.560
The first thing that you're going to want to&nbsp;
do is open up Roblox Studio. You can open up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:39.280
one of your existing projects, but for the sake of&nbsp;
this tutorial, I'll just create a new experience.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.720
Have the AI assistant open right here. And I'm now&nbsp;
going to show you method one, which requires you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:52.560
to prompt it. Go over to the three dots right here&nbsp;
and press manage skills. Then click create new.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.520
I'll just paste in a prompt that I already&nbsp;
typed in earlier. When writing out your prompt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:02.640
first state what you want the skill to be called.&nbsp;
Then describe how you want the skill to function.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:09.280
And you could also explain how you want the skill&nbsp;
to be formatted. But that's completely optional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:18.640
since Roblox's default model will probably handle&nbsp;
it just fine. And I'm now going to send my prompt.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:35.760
If we go back to the three dots right here and&nbsp;
click manage skills, we can verify that has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:41.840
successfully created the Roblox lead system&nbsp;
architect skill I asked for. If you'd like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:50.000
to edit your skill, select a skill, press open,&nbsp;
make sure that this editor toggle is turned on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:56.480
and you can begin changing the specific details&nbsp;
of your skill. If you want to delete your skill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:02.160
then select the skill that you want to be deleted&nbsp;
and press the delete button right here. Method one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:08.240
is better in my opinion because it's fast, easy,&nbsp;
and you can still fix mistakes later. But if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:13.440
want absolute control over the first draft,&nbsp;
then method two is probably better for you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:19.840
which I'm about to show you now. Go over to the&nbsp;
three dots right here and click manage skills.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:28.560
Then click add. I'll just type in Roblox&nbsp;
lead systems architect skill. Now write a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:35.280
description for your skill. I'll just paste in a&nbsp;
description I already wrote. Then click create.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:41.200
Click on the open button right here and make sure&nbsp;
that editor mode is toggled on. Write what your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:47.360
skill does here. The agent reads this content when&nbsp;
it invokes your skill. But because I already made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:53.360
this skill before, I'll just go over here and&nbsp;
paste it in just like that. Once you're done,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:59.760
click save and press the X icon next to your&nbsp;
skills name. I'm going to compare the Roblox&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:06.080
AI assistant without my custom skill to the&nbsp;
Roblox AI assistant with my custom skill. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:12.160
Roblox lead systems architect skill is going&nbsp;
to be disabled. So, we can test how the Roblox&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.840
AI assistant would normally respond. If you&nbsp;
go into the chat bar right here and type in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:30.160
can you make the tool in starter pack damage&nbsp;
the clone of my Roblox avatar? Play a sparkling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:42.320
effect for everyone and track the amount of&nbsp;
times I killed my clone in leader stats. All

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:14.720
Alright, the original Roblox AI assistant is done.&nbsp;
I have this other experience open right here. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:20.560
I'm just gonna go ahead and copy&nbsp;
and paste this prompt right here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:33.200
into the chat of this experience right&nbsp;
here. And I'm going to press enter.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:45.760
The custom skill AI assistant is also done.&nbsp;
Let's see if there's any differences. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.760 --> 00:05:00.080
I'm just going to make this [music] full&nbsp;
screen so it's easier to see for you guys.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:07.040
All right. For some reason, the custom skill&nbsp;
AI assistant didn't invoke the skill. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:12.720
if you're ever in the situation, just&nbsp;
simply ask it, can you use the whatever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:29.280
your skill is called to update the&nbsp;
scripts or whatever you want updated.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:48.240
And as we can see here, the custom skill AI&nbsp;
assistant has finally listened and called the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:54.000
skill my Roblox lead systems architect&nbsp;
skill. Listened to its instructions.

